# condor_submit_dag sweep_components_rawccf.dag : sweep_components.dag again with ccf_norm = 2 (CCF_NORM of
# settings_components.sh: raw ring CCFs, the brightness of the spots and faculae and the limb darkening in the RV),
# for every spot bisector of bisectors_components.txt and every line of parameters_components.txt. The identification
# and the filling factors of the parts are those of sweep_components.dag (ident and aggregate are not run again), the
# confs, grids, simulations and results go to the folders with the suffix _rawccf in ${BASE}/components:
#   0. the lists of the jobs (SCRIPT PRE jobs_components.sh)
#   1. the grids of every Temp, one job per bisector (build_grids_components.sub)
#   2. one job per line and bisector: the simulation of the 5 parts, stats.json of the totals (run_components.sub)
#   3. tables and figures of the totals (collect_components.sub; it runs even if some sets failed)
# Not at the same time as the other sweep_components*.dag: they write the same lists of jobs.
JOB grids    build_grids_components.sub
JOB sets     run_components.sub
JOB collect  collect_components.sub
SCRIPT PRE grids /bin/bash jobs_components.sh
PARENT grids CHILD sets
PARENT sets  CHILD collect
SCRIPT POST sets /bin/true
